*> LINKAGE records used without an address. USING parameters, ENTRY
*> parameters, SET ADDRESS OF, ALLOCATE, members and redefinitions of
*> addressed records, and constants are fine.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. LINKS.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  BUFFER-PTR         USAGE POINTER.
LINKAGE SECTION.
78  MAX-LEN            VALUE 10.
01  PARM-A.
    05  PARM-A-KEY     PIC X(4).
01  PARM-A-ALT REDEFINES PARM-A PIC X(4).
01  ENTRY-B            PIC X(10).
01  BUFFER-C           PIC X(MAX-LEN).
01  ALLOC-D            PIC X(10).
01  LOST-E.
    05  LOST-E-KEY     PIC X(4).
01  NEVER-USED-F       PIC X(10).
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING PARM-A.
MAIN-LINE.
    SET ADDRESS OF BUFFER-C TO BUFFER-PTR
    ALLOCATE ALLOC-D
    DISPLAY PARM-A-KEY PARM-A-ALT BUFFER-C ALLOC-D
    DISPLAY LOST-E-KEY
    MOVE SPACES TO LOST-E
    GOBACK.
ALT-ENTRY.
    ENTRY "LINKSB" USING ENTRY-B
    DISPLAY ENTRY-B
    GOBACK.
